          %h2#foundational_issues Foundational issues
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            has a radix expansion. However, one does have the following results:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In the presence of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+countable+choice"} weak countable choice
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} there exists
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radix+notation"} radix expansion
                in any base (e.g., a decimal expansion or binary expansion) for every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+number"} Cauchy real number
                iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LLPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LLPO}_\mathbb{N}
                holds; there exists a radix expansion for every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+number"} Dedekind real number
                has iff the analytic
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LLPO
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LLPO}
                holds. Without
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+countable+choice"} weak countable choice
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lifschitz+realizability"} Lifschitz realizability
                gives a model in which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LLPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LLPO}_\mathbb{N}
                holds but it is not true that there exists a radix expansion in any base for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+number"} Cauchy real number
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+number"} Dedekind real number
                = succeed "\u2018s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Swan"} Andrew Swan
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#Swan"} Birchfield (2024)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LLPO
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LLPO}
                holds for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+sets"} condensed sets
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟚
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2}
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant function
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+number"} Dedekind real number
            %li
              %p
                In the presence of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+choice"} countable choice
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LLPO
                        %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{LLPO}_\mathbb{N}
                is equivalent to the claim that the rings of radix expansions in any two bases are isomorphic. See Daniel Mehkeri's answer to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#Mehkeri"} Feldman (2010)
            %li
              %p
                That every Cauchy real number has a choice of radix expansion in any base implies that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+limited+principle+of+omniscience"} weak limited principle of omniscience
                (WLPO) for the natural numbers holds; that every Dedekind real number has a choice of radix expansion implies that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+WLPO"} analytic WLPO
                holds.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Richman"} Fred Richman
            considered a number system (a noncancellable
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                    %mover
                      %mn 9
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0.\overline{9} \lt 1
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Richman1999"} Richman 1999
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                  %mover
                    %mn 9
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0.\overline{9}
            is not cancellable, and there is no value of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                    %mover
                      %mn 9
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 - 0.\overline{9}
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperreal+number"} hyperreal number
            has a radix expansion (by the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfer+principle"} transfer principle
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 10
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 10
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                  %mover
                    %mn 9
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0.\overline{9} \lt 1
            if it is understood that the bar applies a hyperfinite but nonstandard number of places (although
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                    %mover
                      %mn 9
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0.\overline{9} = 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                    %mover
                      %mn 9
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                    %mover
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ¯
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 - 0.\overline{9} = 0.\overline{0}1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                  %mover
                    %mn 9
                    %mo ¯
                  %mn 9
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                  %mover
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ¯
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 - 0.\overline{9}9 = 0.\overline{0}1
            would be more accurate. Of course, one could write this same equation in standard mathematics if the bar is understood to apply to a large but finite number of places. (Note that it’s not possible to have the bar apply to
            %em exactly
            the standard places, since the set of standard natural numbers is not definable. Indeed, in that case the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            would have to be at the least nonstandard place, and there is no such number.)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"}> real numbers
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irrational+numbers"} irrational numbers
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+LPO"}> analytic LPO
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+WLPO"} analytic WLPO
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+decimal+representation+of+a+unit+interval"} infinite decimal representation of a unit interval
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p#Abian1981
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Alexander Abian
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Alexander+Abian"} ?
                \. 1981. Calculus must consist of the study of real numbers in their decimal representation and not of the study of an abstract complete ordered field or nonstandard real numbers. International Journal of Mathematical Education in Science and Technology 12(4).
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/0020739810120417"} Doi:10.1080/0020739810120417
            %li#Nicholas92
              %p Nichols, Eugene D, et al. Holt Algebra with Trigonometry. Holt, Rinehart and Winston : Harcourt Brace Jovanovich, 1992.
            %li#Marecek20
              %p Marecek, Lynn, et al. Prealgebra 2e. OpenStax, Rice University, 2020.
            %li
              %p#Richman1999
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Richman"}> Fred Richman
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Is 0.999… = 1?
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/0025570X.1999.11996777"} doi:10.1080/0025570X.1999.11996777
            %li#Mehkeri
              %p
                David Feldman (2010) on Math.Overflow,
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/49775/radix-notation-and-toposes/"} Radix notation and toposes
            %li#Swan
              %p
                Madeleine Birchfield (2024) on Category Theory Zulip,
